    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.2.07-01",
      "block_type": "definition",
      "heading": "Improving commercial farm output",
      "text": "Farm output can be improved by addressing the factor that limits production. Improved varieties, irrigation, fertilisers and pest management act through different mechanisms. Their effects depend on crop, soil, water, management and affordability. A proposed technology should therefore be judged against a stated aim, such as stable food output, net income or reduced water use. A larger harvest does not by itself establish success against every one of those aims.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "CL-6137-2.2.07-1",
        "CL-6137-2.2.07-2",
        "CL-6137-2.2.07-01-1",
