    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.2.07-04",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Genetically modified crops have genetic material altered using genetic-engineering methods. Genetic modification is a technique, not a single crop characteristic. A particular crop may have a trait intended to resist a specified insect, tolerate a herbicide or address another production problem. The relevant question is whether that trait helps under the stated conditions. An insect-resistance trait does not supply water, prevent every disease or establish that all genetically modified crops have higher yields.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "CL-6137-2.2.07-1",
        "CL-6137-2.2.07-2",
        "CL-6137-2.2.07-01-1",
        "CL-6137-2.2.07-01-2",
