    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.2.07-05",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "A relevant benefit occurs when a trait reduces a loss that would otherwise limit production. If a specific insect is causing substantial damage and a suitable resistant crop reduces that damage, usable harvest may rise. Performance must be monitored, and suitable resistance-management practices are needed because pest populations can change over time. Seed cost, access, approved use, management requirements and market acceptance may also influence whether the choice meets a farm's stated objective.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "CL-6137-2.2.07-1",
        "CL-6137-2.2.07-2",
        "CL-6137-2.2.07-01-1",
        "CL-6137-2.2.07-01-2",
