    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.2.07-06",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Avoid confusing genetic modification with ordinary selective breeding or with every high-yielding variety. Conventional breeding selects and crosses plants to develop useful inherited characteristics; genetic engineering uses different methods to alter genetic material. A high-yielding variety may have been produced without genetic engineering. These categories overlap in possible outcomes but are not synonyms. Evaluate the actual trait, evidence and growing requirements instead of assuming that a technical label describes the whole farming system.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "CL-6137-2.2.07-1",
        "CL-6137-2.2.07-2",
