    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.2.07-08",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Different application methods have different implications. Surface irrigation distributes water across the soil; sprinklers spray it; drip systems deliver smaller flows near plants through emitters. Drip can reduce some evaporation or unnecessary wetting compared with poorly managed alternatives, but requires appropriate design, filtration and maintenance. Blocked emitters can leave plants short of water. Choose a method using the crop, soil, slope, water quality, available capital and operating capacity rather than calling one method ideal everywhere.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "CL-6137-2.2.07-1",
        "CL-6137-2.2.07-2",
        "CL-6137-2.2.07-01-1",
        "CL-6137-2.2.07-01-2",
