    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.2.07-09",
      "block_type": "worked_application",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Water efficiency and total use are separate. If a system needs less water per hectare but the irrigated area expands, total abstraction may still rise. Suppose application falls from 1,000 to 700 cubic metres per hectare for the stated interval, while area rises from two to four hectares. Total application changes from 2,000 to 2,800 cubic metres. Efficiency per hectare improved in this narrow comparison, but the total volume increased. A resource-management judgement needs both measures and the source's sustainable availability.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "CL-6137-2.2.07-1",
        "CL-6137-2.2.07-2",
