    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.2.07-10",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Irrigation can also create waterlogging or salinisation where drainage and water management are unsuitable. Evaporation and plant water use leave salts behind; a shallow saline water table can supply additional salts to the root zone. Rising salt concentration can make water uptake more difficult and reduce crop performance. Prevention may require suitable drainage, water quality assessment and appropriately managed leaching where conditions allow. Adding more water without drainage can worsen rather than resolve the problem.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "CL-6137-2.2.07-1",
