    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.2.07-11",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Fertilisers supply plant nutrients. A suitable nutrient application can relieve a deficiency and support growth, but crops also require adequate water, suitable soil conditions and protection from serious damage. Applying a nutrient already present in sufficient quantity may bring little benefit. Soil information and crop requirements help select the type, amount and timing. The goal is usable nutrient supply, not simply the largest possible application rate.",
      "claim_ids": [
