      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.2.07-12",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Mineral fertilisers can provide relatively concentrated nutrients in known formulations. They may be easier to apply precisely than bulky organic materials, but purchase cost and loss pathways matter. Excess or poorly timed application can allow nutrients to reach water through runoff or leaching. Nutrient enrichment can stimulate excessive algal growth; subsequent decay uses oxygen and can harm aquatic organisms. Appropriate rate, timing and placement link the production benefit to reduced waste and pollution risk.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "CL-6137-2.2.07-1",
        "CL-6137-2.2.07-2",
        "CL-6137-2.2.07-01-1",
