      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.2.07-13",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Organic fertilisers such as suitably managed manure and compost can return nutrients and organic matter. Their nutrient content and release rate vary with material and decomposition conditions. They may improve soil structure and water retention as well as nutrient supply, but they still need suitable handling and application. The words organic and natural do not establish that a material is harmless, nutrient-balanced or sufficient for a particular crop. These options are developed further in the sustainable-agriculture section.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "CL-6137-2.2.07-1",
        "CL-6137-2.2.07-2",
        "CL-6137-2.2.07-01-1",
        "CL-6137-2.2.07-01-2",
