    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.2.07-14",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Pesticides are substances used to control pests; different products target different organisms. Insecticides target insects, herbicides weeds and fungicides fungi. A suitable intervention can reduce a specific loss, but a product chosen for one target does not solve every pest problem. Application must be appropriate to the pest and crop, with safe handling and relevant instructions. This geographical discussion explains production and environmental effects; it is not a set of application directions.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "CL-6137-2.2.07-1",
        "CL-6137-2.2.07-2",
        "CL-6137-2.2.07-01-1",
        "CL-6137-2.2.07-01-2",
