    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.2.07-15",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Repeated reliance on the same control can favour resistant pests. Some treatments can also harm non-target organisms, including beneficial predators or pollinators, depending on the substance and exposure. Integrated pest management combines monitoring with appropriate cultural, biological and, where needed, chemical measures. It aims to manage damaging populations while avoiding unnecessary treatments. Monitoring distinguishes a real damaging outbreak from the mere presence of an organism that does not justify intervention.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "CL-6137-2.2.07-1",
        "CL-6137-2.2.07-2",
        "CL-6137-2.2.07-01-1",
        "CL-6137-2.2.07-01-2",
