    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.2.07-18",
      "block_type": "worked_application",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "A good judgement also considers reliability. One favourable season may not reveal how a variety performs in dry conditions or whether equipment can be repaired locally. Compare results over suitable conditions and time, with the same crop and units. Yield records, input costs, water use and relevant environmental observations answer different parts of the decision. The preferred strategy is the one supported against the stated criterion under the stated constraints, rather than whichever has the most modern name.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "CL-6137-2.2.07-1",
        "CL-6137-2.2.07-2",
