    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.2.07-19",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "The appropriate evidence depends on the improvement claim. To test whether irrigation stabilises production, compare yield variation through wet and dry periods alongside water availability. To test a nutrient response, compare crops receiving different suitable treatments while accounting for water, variety and field conditions. A single high yield after several changes cannot identify which change produced the gain. It supports the combined outcome, with uncertainty about the contribution of each component.",
