    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-2.2.07-20",
      "block_type": "cross_link",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "A hypothetical pest-resistant variety gives 2.5 tonnes per hectare where a susceptible comparison gives two tonnes under the stated insect pressure. That is a 0.5-tonne difference, or 25% relative to the comparison. The result concerns those conditions. If a separate trial has no target pest and both yield two tonnes, the trait has not produced an observed yield advantage there. This does not contradict its value where the target damage actually occurs.",
